content.text:
Now the mobile garage looks good! So the earlier black screenshot was a timing artifact (panel animation/opacity) — screenshot captured too soon at 500ms with slow compositing. The garage layout on mobile: panel fills almost entire screen, scrolls; title and cash; stage list; shop; footer hint cut off at bottom (needs scroll). There is a scrollbar visible on right. The launch button is below the fold; user scrolls. Acceptable, though having the primary "LOAD TEST" button below the fold is not ideal. We could make the garage footer sticky at bottom of the panel so the launch button is always visible while content scrolls. Currently `.garage-panel` scrolls as a whole (max-height 94dvh, overflow-y auto on mobile). The footer with the launch button is at the very bottom after shop; user must scroll. That's a UX concern on mobile. But the panel height 793 and content 869, only 78px overflow; scroll down reveals footer. Fine but "LOAD TEST" primary action hidden initially. Could improve by making garage footer sticky bottom within the scrolling panel:

```
@media (max-width: 980px) {
  .garage-foot {
    position: sticky;
    bottom: -1px;
    background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(8,12,15,0.7), rgba(8,12,15,0.98));
    margin-top: 12px;
    padding: 12px 0 2px;
    backdrop-filter: blur? no (perf)
    z-index: 2;
  }
}
```

But panel background is gradient, sticky footer would cover content while scrolling. It would ensure launch visible. However, footer hint + button stacked (mobile) takes ~76px. With only 78px overflow, that would shrink the visible content area slightly but still scroll. Might be good.

