  background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(7,11,14,0.55), rgba(7,11,14,0.99) 40%);
}
```
But `.garage-panel` has padding 24px 26px; mobile panel padding 20px 16px from 620 query. `padding-bottom: 0` then footer has its own bottom. The footer width matches content. Good.

Also on mobile, `.garage-head` flex-direction column at max-width 620; at 390 yes. The title + cash/close stacked. Fine.

At 620-980 (tablet), garage-head remains row; footer sticky still. Fine.

Sticky footer over content: add box-shadow above? `box-shadow: 0 -10px 24px rgba(0,0,0,0.35);` maybe. Keep subtle.

